WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.470
- And speaking of Nashville,

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:04.098
you had country music star ambitions,

00:00:04.098 --> 00:00:06.470
you wanted to be a country
singer and I had no idea.

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:07.303
- I did.

00:00:07.303 --> 00:00:08.990
Kelly, as wild as that sounds,

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:10.510
and you'll appreciate this, obviously,

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.110
because of your love for music

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:13.840
and certainly country music too.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:17.380
I grew up loving blues, hip hop, of course

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:19.670
but then country, but
real traditional country,

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:22.280
like that three chords and the truth,

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:23.690
steel guitar kind of country.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:28.690
And when I got to Nashville,
I started hanging out,

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:30.560
because I didn't have a lot of friends,

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.130
because they all thought
I was an undercover cop.

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:35.170
So, I started hanging out on Broad Street,

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:37.040
and you know Broad
Street where Tootsies is

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:38.550
and the Ryman Auditorium,

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:39.760
and I loved country music--
- On Broadway, yeah.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:44.760
- At that time and I had
this fantasy in my head.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:45.920
So, the story goes like this.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:49.120
I was at a grocery store
and I was shopping,

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:49.970
and when I say shopping,

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:52.080
I was actually doing a
little five-finger discount,

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:54.160
at that time, because I
couldn't afford anything.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:58.580
So, and I was in the middle of the row

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:03.610
in the shopping aisle, and
I was belting out this song,

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:05.590
not caring who was listening to me.

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:07.570
And then, a woman comes around the corner

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:09.250
and she sticks her head around the corner

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:12.250
and she looks, and I stopped singing.

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:15.367
She looks at me, her eyes
go wide and she's like,

00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:19.127
"Wow, I did not expect to see

00:01:19.127 --> 00:01:23.130
"someone who looks like
you singing that song."

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:24.690
And I said, "Oh, thank you."

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:27.657
And then we had this
chat and she was like,

00:01:27.657 --> 00:01:30.837
(laughs) she goes, "So clearly,

00:01:30.837 --> 00:01:32.307
"you should go down to Broad Street,

00:01:32.307 --> 00:01:34.190
"'cause that's where the
country singers are."

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:35.410
- On Broadway, yeah.
- I didn't tell her I was 15

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:37.320
and I had no business being
in a bar at that time.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:38.650
But then, I went down
there, on Broad Street,

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:39.680
and I used to hang out down there

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:42.160
and listen to all the acts
and I did have it in my mind

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:46.500
that I was gonna become
a country music singer.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.860
Then, I realized that singing in keys

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:52.300
that don't exist might not
be (laughs) of good value.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:54.130
- No, you can't say that.

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:54.963
You're so full of it.

00:01:54.963 --> 00:01:56.410
You were great in "Moana."

00:01:56.410 --> 00:01:57.530
I was like, "What?"

00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:59.960
I had no idea. So then, when
I found out the country thing,

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:02.077
I was like, "Oh, and you
married a singer/songwriter.

00:02:02.077 --> 00:02:03.317
"This is all starting to make sense

00:02:03.317 --> 00:02:05.470
"of where your career is headed."

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:06.690
So, here's my thing.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:08.170
We sing on this show a lot.

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:10.020
So, I'm just saying if you
and your wife just stop by,

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:11.560
like we should all sing together sometime.

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:13.440
I'm just saying, or on cheat
day, we'll just hang out.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:15.430
- We've got to, we gotta
do, let's do it, I'm down.

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:16.603
Let's do a duet.
- I'm down.

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:18.280
♪ Islands in the stream ♪

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.030
There we go. I am down.

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:21.110
I have done that.

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:23.150
Well, actually, the only
time I've sing that song

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:24.708
is drunk at a karaoke bar.

00:02:24.708 --> 00:02:26.020
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:28.227
I don't think I've remember
sang that song sober.

00:02:28.227 --> 00:02:29.350
That's fine.

